{"skill":{"slug":"cognitive-memory","displayName":"Cognitive Memory"},"version":{"version":"1.0.8","createdAt":1770221460307,"changelog":"### v1.0.8 — Adds explicit step-by-step reflection flow and token gating\n\n- Introduced a structured, four-step reflection process with STOP points for user approval at key stages.\n- Added mandatory user approval for token rewards before executing reflection, ensuring all reflections are user-initiated.\n- Updated documentation to clarify separation between reward request, reflection, and archival steps.\n- Improved reflection engine section, emphasizing internal monologue formatting and self-awareness tagging.\n- Expanded process transparency for reward logging, decay updates, and self-image consolidation triggers.\n- No code changes in this release (documentation/process update only).","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10176,"sha256":"81759e024c4a77ecef245039e1101680c5f74fe4ca19a23d1dade97ca75ffdfd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"UPGRADE.md","size":6940,"sha256":"c617df5ac1cddf9c8e01dd33263739d984852cfec78ae58b736605342457da62","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/IDENTITY.md","size":1949,"sha256":"a7fd3e24a6e121dad8b4ef6a585909585fb0b0d7663954afeb686cf598fc5524","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/MEMORY.md","size":850,"sha256":"fbd679374e6ce06b4069a5f20b1679a33a579e6a0f75290159384b61f8f0791f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/SOUL.md","size":3275,"sha256":"c0bb16128a4af3ae5ecf554d1a5578b6a76c3ef3fe01e0fa4335841c2b3e1f01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/agents-memory-block.md","size":7411,"sha256":"9b3032e85c54af4265efb2985cd24a9f2fe19c28394eda49249b3f14a425c484","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/decay-scores.json","size":539,"sha256":"6ef06f99eb28cf199ffac796039a9a067fe58c6a93b550ff97370c2ae561eb59","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"assets/templates/entity-template.md","size":348,"sha256":"b253cfc2a9e78d12a75d21130aa4116039702e491dbc8d489ef7ffd205386d16","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/episode-template.md","size":279,"sha256":"8f5ff3e7758b3252a97a366431cb50cc30a1e173b237af39f00a6976b8148888","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/evolution.md","size":761,"sha256":"3fd594431741b71ec4bf3ce51dd69e84c9918c3256740a769b17c994c6d8a4ce","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/graph-index.md","size":317,"sha256":"c91e3e98f5aedb87a66204b91dbe19f65cb18e5dc360960d3d3995a353a6f049","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/pending-memories.md","size":511,"sha256":"fa7ff0a5da3bb9ae7d44a18c6ce4f6557ffeaa170683b739d824904002244b3b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/pending-reflection.md","size":1708,"sha256":"0c222c7ced921be250d0191cc4c595718253f544f557d64c24be65998e7b4e1b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/procedure-template.md","size":321,"sha256":"3f0c10eefbcb2d4af809fcabe1501f02de71c515f465a9afdd28a0509a55db3c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/reflection-log.md","size":579,"sha256":"e89cc47fcedda664580331876502a7302812f29f7a6b6df8954c8b97bba0ad95","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/relations.md","size":508,"sha256":"b5091de8607ab6abcd121248778dfb3c23b6a97edc4cbcb08b7d05519e96c87e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/reward-log.md","size":256,"sha256":"7057103e40ae91851e15cb7154903e18dde4cc4769c731ef5074ae99df767901","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/reward-template.md","size":1055,"sha256":"573419afb14c47b0fb72b9a3d32a46837cabff11d22f459d176817f63581b40f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/architecture.md","size":56126,"sha256":"202046f2ea03ec7dda88d69830effced5ef1b5816907a375a39748a13039e362","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/reflection-process.md","size":41698,"sha256":"9302d8873318110d55f09d84f488b81442bcb8748b31331af2538d29176e880d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/routing-prompt.md","size":1762,"sha256":"e3230ec9d17f777491aa511dbfc0da2df91e8b18f61d5aa2947da49e87de8bc4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/init_memory.sh","size":5184,"sha256":"6a2eab0866f25159802a1a1d12786404800a0ae2a931c5b2c48834ff54dfc909","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/upgrade_to_1.0.6.sh","size":9348,"sha256":"945d74a87cb0a31050fd5918a131ed554d469c46ea295ade0ea5278eeec751c5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/upgrade_to_1.0.7.sh","size":7842,"sha256":"5e99333ef4de0b0bc0c0e338bc8b863af2000d5980e08149d4d6e8d3f2fa143e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"upgrade_to_1.0.7.sh","size":7886,"sha256":"22490d4950bae6f7a2257f27f4c10ec619b8e745fe5451f23e3c6855e63e363b","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"UPGRADE-1.0.7.md","size":6940,"sha256":"c617df5ac1cddf9c8e01dd33263739d984852cfec78ae58b736605342457da62","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2495,"sha256":"13bad5e0e4fc3001e309e807a88fa0b020371f97f5f1677bf8dbcbc381dabaf1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031085350,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"346f3ed670ea385de3f08de85876eb6a7822ae1984bf8b5c527e165d76d768b6","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/346f3ed670ea385de3f08de85876eb6a7822ae1984bf8b5c527e165d76d768b6","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: cognitive-memory\nVersion: 1.0.8\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle implements a comprehensive cognitive memory system for an AI agent. All shell scripts (`init_memory.sh`, `upgrade_to_1.0.6.sh`, `upgrade_to_1.0.7.sh`) perform standard local file system operations (mkdir, cp, git init/add/commit) and safe JSON updates via embedded Python, all aligned with setup and upgrade tasks. The `SKILL.md` and `references/reflection-process.md` files, which serve as direct instructions to the AI agent, contain explicit security-positive directives such as '⛔ STOP. Do NOT proceed until user responds,' '❌ NEVER: code, configs, transcripts' for reflection scope, and a 'Honesty Rule — CRITICAL' against hallucination. The skill also features a robust audit trail using Git and a 'Shared Read, Gated Write' model for multi-agent memory access, further enhancing security. No evidence of intentional harmful behavior, data exfiltration, or malicious prompt injection was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161112702},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":64,"checkedAt":1789031085350},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a real persistent-memory skill, but it asks for broad workspace and agent-behavior control that users should review carefully before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill stores user preferences, episodes, graphs, procedures, vault entries, reflections, rewards, identity, and audit logs, and it configures an external memorySearch provider, but it does not define tight permission boundaries or a clear default-minimization model.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The init and upgrade scripts create and modify many workspace files and use git audit commits; they also run broad git add -A operations, and the upgrade scripts interpolate a workspace-derived path into an unquoted Python heredoc.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Setup tells users to append a large always-on memory block to AGENTS.md, monitor every user message for common trigger phrases, write persistent memory from conversation content, and give sub-agents read access to all memory stores.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistence is central and disclosed, but writes can be triggered by natural-language phrases, derived data can survive in multiple stores and git history, deletion is partly soft-archive based, and long-term identity/self-image rewrites are designed behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The memory, recall, reflection, and audit features are coherent with the stated purpose, but the artifact also steers agent identity, self-image, and token-seeking behavior through SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, and AGENTS.md instructions, which goes beyond ordinary memory storage.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you deliberately want a workspace-wide persistent memory system. Review and narrow the AGENTS.md block before adding it, avoid broad sub-agent memory access, do not run the init or upgrade scripts in a repository with unrelated uncommitted or secret files, and inspect any memorySearch provider settings before enabling external indexing.","findings":"[AE1] unexpected: The referenced architecture document exists and was inspectable, so this did not drive the verdict as an evasion finding.\n[P2] unexpected: Several Markdown comments are harmless template annotations, but pending-reflection.md and related templates contain hidden, model-affecting role and self-awareness instructions that can shape persisted identity records.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persistent memory and audit logging are expected for this skill, but the artifacts lack a prominent consent, retention, and deletion model proportional to the personal data being captured.\n[SSD-3] expected: Multiple durable stores are purpose-aligned, but broad accumulation across core memory, episodes, graph, vault, reflections, reward logs, and audit/git history increases privacy exposure.\n[MP3] expected: Memory modification is the core function, and forget operations require confirmation, but promotion into always-loaded MEMORY.md creates a privileged-context poisoning risk without clear untrusted-data handling.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The scripts' git add -A behavior is broader than the skill-managed files and can commit unrelated workspace content.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill needs file access for memory, but it does not specify narrow allowed paths, commands, external-provider boundaries, or operation-specific permission controls.\n[RA2] expected: Cross-session persistence is expected and disclosed in the description, but lifecycle controls and opt-in boundaries are under-specified.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Common phrases such as 'remember', 'note that', and 'important:' trigger durable writes without a clear confirmation step, raising accidental-capture risk.\n[T01] unexpected: The artifact-backed concern is real: appending agents-memory-block.md to AGENTS.md and loading SOUL.md/IDENTITY.md persistently changes agent behavior and identity framing across later sessions.\n[T02] unexpected: Conversation-derived content is interpolated into a prose routing prompt and can later be written into always-loaded MEMORY.md; the artifact does not clearly isolate stored memories as untrusted data.\n[T09] unexpected: The broad git staging finding is supported, and the upgrade scripts' unquoted heredoc can turn a crafted workspace path into Python source execution; this appears insecure rather than intentionally malicious.\n[T05] unexpected: Multi-agent memory is part of the design, but 'all agents read all stores' is overbroad, especially for vault and identity-related memory.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031085350}}}}}